cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research prototype, please cite the software using the
  metadata in this file and reference the exact version or commit used.
title: Agent-Assisted Cesium Digital Twin Research Prototype
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khot
    given-names: Vijay
    email: vijaysinh.khot@gmail.com
    affiliation: Louisiana State University
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/vijaybkhot/agentic-cesium-digital-twin
url: https://github.com/vijaybkhot/agentic-cesium-digital-twin
abstract: >-
  A research prototype for interoperable urban digital-twin visualization in
  CesiumJS and ArcGIS, with local OpenStreetMap, FEMA National Flood Hazard
  Layer, and USGS 3D Elevation Program data-processing and provenance
  workflows. The repository also contains mock application modes and interface
  boundaries for future reconstruction and agent integrations. It is not a
  production system, official hazard determination, or source of emergency
  guidance.
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - CesiumJS
  - ArcGIS
  - geospatial visualization
  - OpenStreetMap
  - FEMA
  - USGS 3DEP
  - urban resilience
  - data provenance
